Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:17:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Fix control circle: menu jump, landscape crash and drag
 handling

- The menu used to open 192dp to the left of the circle and draw the circle at
  its right edge, so a circle on the left half of the screen (or near the top
  or bottom) jumped when the menu opened. The menu now opens towards the middle
  of the screen and the circle is drawn exactly where it was.
- Opening the menu in landscape threw IllegalArgumentException (coerceIn with a
  negative upper bound) and crashed the service. Bounds are clamped, and the
  menu rows shrink when the screen is too short for the full menu.
- A drag starts after the system touch slop (was 4dp, below normal finger
  jitter, so some taps did not open the menu) and the circle only follows the
  finger once it is dragging.
- The position is saved when the drag ends instead of on every move event.
- A cancelled touch ends the drag cleanly.
